---
/**
 * Best SNPs per cohort, divided by the LD decay length, against the LD decay
 * length.
 *
 * The horizontal line is the rule quoted above it: best SNPs per cohort is
 * 3.3 times the LD decay length. The points are the ten measured optima in
 * proofs/validation/differential/cluster/partition_curve_results.json under
 * "general_optimum", one per correlation between neighbouring SNPs, where the
 * LD decay length is one over one minus that correlation.
 */
const measured = [
  { rho: 0.5, len: 2.0, best: 7, ratio: 3.5 },
  { rho: 0.7, len: 3.333333333333333, best: 11, ratio: 3.3000000000000003 },
  { rho: 0.8, len: 5.000000000000001, best: 17, ratio: 3.3999999999999995 },
  { rho: 0.9, len: 10.000000000000002, best: 33, ratio: 3.2999999999999994 },
  { rho: 0.95, len: 19.999999999999982, best: 66, ratio: 3.300000000000003 },
  { rho: 0.98, len: 49.99999999999996, best: 164, ratio: 3.280000000000003 },
  { rho: 0.99, len: 99.99999999999991, best: 328, ratio: 3.280000000000003 },
  { rho: 0.995, len: 199.99999999999983, best: 655, ratio: 3.2750000000000026 },
  { rho: 0.999, len: 999.9999999999991, best: 3272, ratio: 3.272000000000003 },
  { rho: 0.9995, len: 2000.0000000002203, best: 6543, ratio: 3.2714999999996395 },
];

const RULE = 3.3;

const W = 760, H = 300, L = 62, R = 24, T = 18, B = 48;
const iw = W - L - R, ih = H - T - B;
const lx = Math.log10;
const x0 = lx(1.5), x1 = lx(3000), y0 = 3.15, y1 = 3.6;
const X = (v: number) => L + ((lx(v) - x0) / (x1 - x0)) * iw;
const Y = (v: number) => H - B - ((v - y0) / (y1 - y0)) * ih;
---

<figure class="fig">
  <figcaption class="fig-title">
    The best cohort holds 3.3 LD decay lengths of SNPs, over a thousandfold range
    of LD decay length
  </figcaption>
  <svg viewBox={`0 0 ${W} ${H}`} role="img"
       aria-label="Best SNPs per cohort divided by the LD decay length, against the LD decay length. Ten measured optima lie between 3.27 and 3.50 across LD decay lengths from 2 to 2000 SNPs.">
    {[3.2, 3.3, 3.4, 3.5].map((v) => (
      <>
        <line x1={L} x2={W - R} y1={Y(v)} y2={Y(v)} class="grid" />
        <text x={L - 10} y={Y(v) + 4} class="tick" text-anchor="end">{v.toFixed(1)}</text>
      </>
    ))}
    {[2, 5, 10, 50, 100, 500, 1000, 2000].map((v) => (
      <text x={X(v)} y={H - B + 20} class="tick" text-anchor="middle">{v.toLocaleString()}</text>
    ))}
    <text x={L + iw / 2} y={H - 10} class="axis" text-anchor="middle">
      LD decay length, in SNPs
    </text>
    <text x={16} y={T + ih / 2} class="axis" text-anchor="middle"
          transform={`rotate(-90 16 ${T + ih / 2})`}>best SNPs per cohort, per LD decay length</text>

    <line x1={L} x2={W - R} y1={Y(RULE)} y2={Y(RULE)} class="curve" />
    {measured.map((d) => <circle cx={X(d.len)} cy={Y(d.ratio)} r="5.5" class="dot" />)}

    <g class="legend">
      <line x1={W - R - 168} x2={W - R - 140} y1={T + 10} y2={T + 10} class="curve" />
      <text x={W - R - 132} y={T + 14} class="tick">the rule, 3.3</text>
      <circle cx={W - R - 154} cy={T + 30} r="5.5" class="dot" />
      <text x={W - R - 132} y={T + 34} class="tick">measured optimum</text>
    </g>
  </svg>
  <p class="fig-note">
    The LD decay length here is one over one minus the correlation between
    neighbouring SNPs, and it runs from 2 SNPs to 2,000. The best cohort holds 7
    SNPs at the short end and 6,543 at the long end, and every ratio between
    those two lies in 3.27 to 3.50. Across the same sweep the product of the
    total SNP count, the LD decay length and the error stays between 15.2 and
    16.1, so a population with longer-range linkage disequilibrium needs fewer
    SNPs in total for the same accuracy even though each of its cohorts holds
    more.
  </p>
</figure>
